#
# SVR4 prototype for RDVTagent. Paths are relative to BASEDIR (/opt/rdeskvint),
# so this package is relocatable with `pkgadd -a` or an admin file, and it owns
# nothing outside its own directory.
#
# That is deliberate. Everything this package could put in /etc -- an rc script,
# an rc link, a CDE session hook -- is installed by rdeskvint-enable instead and
# taken away by rdeskvint-disable. So `pkgadd` is inert: it drops files on the
# disk and the machine behaves exactly as it did before. Nothing starts, nothing
# is disabled, and nothing has to be undone if you decide against it.
#
i pkginfo
i postinstall
i preremove
i postremove
#
d none bin 0755 root bin
f none bin/rdeskvint 0755 root bin
f none bin/rdeskvint-enable 0755 root bin
f none bin/rdeskvint-disable 0755 root bin
f none bin/rdeskvint-console-test 0755 root bin
#
# The GCC runtime, which Solaris 9 does not ship and Rust's unwind crate asks
# for by name -- which is why -static-libgcc cannot answer it. The agent carries
# an rpath naming this directory, so a default install needs nothing on
# LD_LIBRARY_PATH. It lives here rather than in /usr/lib/sparcv9 so that it is
# this package's copy for this package's binary, and not a GCC runtime sitting
# in a system directory for some unrelated program to find in a year's time.
d none lib 0755 root bin
f none lib/libgcc_s.so.1 0755 root bin
f none lib/rdeskvint.init 0644 root bin
f none lib/rdeskvint.xsession 0644 root bin
#
d none doc 0755 root bin
f none doc/README.txt 0644 root bin
